.DS_Store

# Conversion output
out/

# SysEx data is not part of this project: see "What this project is not" in the
# README. This line is a safeguard, not a policy statement — dumps of other
# people's patches must never land here by accident. One exception, and it is the
# whole point of it: `examples/example.syx` is a synthetic dump written by
# `examples/make_example.py` beside it, with names that belong to nobody, so the
# captures in the README can be run again. An exemption for anything else would
# need the generator that reproduces it byte for byte.
*.syx
!examples/*.syx
